1
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:11,640
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:20,879 --> 00:00:23,160
You made a mess of this.

3
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,480
I don't need your help.

4
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,239
Put it down.

5
00:00:28,039 --> 00:00:28,839
Okay.

6
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,780
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

7
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:41,719
It's been a long time.

8
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:43,719
Come on in.

9
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,079
Ms. Song.

10
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,560
Mom, this is Qin Ming,

11
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:52,560
your student.

12
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:57,520
Qin Ming?

13
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,560
The one from Class 8?

14
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,079
You were so good at math,

15
00:01:07,079 --> 00:01:09,040
always near the top of your grade,

16
00:01:09,439 --> 00:01:11,959
but not so good at English, right?

17
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:13,560
Yes.

18
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:18,079
Look at the weather.

19
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,120
Will it rain tomorrow?

20
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,760
Have I watered them?

21
00:01:22,079 --> 00:01:24,480
You called her... Mom?

22
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,079
Ms. Song is sick.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,319
She's becoming more forgetful.

24
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:33,519
Have a seat.

25
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:38,560
You've lost weight.

26
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:43,239
You're much thinner
than you were in school.

27
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,280
Is work tough?

28
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,680
Not really.

29
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:52,519
What do you do?

30
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,519
Mom.

31
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,359
The food's getting cold.

32
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:56,519
Let's go eat.

33
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,680
Oh, right.

34
00:01:58,159 --> 00:01:58,959
Let's eat.

35
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:10,380
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 5=

36
00:02:11,599 --> 00:02:12,400
Thank you.

37
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,919
Mom was right.

38
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,840
You are thinner
than you were in high school.

39
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:16,879
Eat more.

40
00:02:16,879 --> 00:02:18,039
You're the same.

41
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,000
Really?

42
00:02:22,759 --> 00:02:23,639
And yet you're different.

43
00:02:24,159 --> 00:02:26,240
I had the class monitor
give you my number.

44
00:02:27,599 --> 00:02:28,919
If I didn't call you,

45
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,439
when were you planning to contact me?

46
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,080
(Jin Keke, I like you.)

47
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:44,240
Were you waiting for the main course?

48
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,599
Yeah!

49
00:02:50,599 --> 00:02:51,319
Qin Ming.

50
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,520
Do you have any questions for me?

51
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,319
Yes.

52
00:02:59,319 --> 00:03:00,319
Too many.

53
00:03:01,039 --> 00:03:02,360
I don't know how to start.

54
00:03:02,439 --> 00:03:03,520
Then let me go first.

55
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,319
You must be wondering

56
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:09,159
why I'm with Ms. Song.

57
00:03:10,599 --> 00:03:11,520
Three years ago,

58
00:03:11,599 --> 00:03:13,080
I ran into her at the hospital.

59
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:15,120
She'd been diagnosed with Alzheimer's.

60
00:03:15,639 --> 00:03:17,120
She was all alone.

61
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,120
And so was I.

62
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:20,919
Two people together

63
00:03:22,439 --> 00:03:23,520
may make things feel warmer.

64
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:25,919
Later,

65
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,439
her condition got worse.

66
00:03:31,199 --> 00:03:32,479
She often mistook me

67
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:35,439
for Xia Wen.

68
00:03:36,199 --> 00:03:37,719
At first, I'd explain.

69
00:03:38,639 --> 00:03:39,439
But later,

70
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,199
I gave up.

71
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:44,960
I just answered
to whatever she called me.

72
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,680
As long as she was happy.

73
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,159
Actually,

74
00:03:50,879 --> 00:03:52,719
I'm glad I can take care of her

75
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,520
in Xia Wen's place.

76
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,759
You dropped out of school

77
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,719
because of Xia Wen?

78
00:03:59,599 --> 00:04:02,080
Qin Ming, all these ten years,

79
00:04:02,639 --> 00:04:04,560
finding out my number
would've been easy.

80
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,960
But you never came looking for me.

81
00:04:08,199 --> 00:04:09,120
And ten years later,

82
00:04:09,879 --> 00:04:11,919
you're still only interested
in what happened back then?

83
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,680
Ten years ago, you just left.

84
00:04:14,759 --> 00:04:16,319
I asked you the same question back then.

85
00:04:17,319 --> 00:04:18,439
You never answered me.

86
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,680
Qin Ming, you should go.

87
00:04:24,399 --> 00:04:25,759
I'm not your suspect.

88
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:28,560
Don't talk to me like that.

89
00:04:30,639 --> 00:04:33,560
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

90
00:04:33,839 --> 00:04:35,360
No one knows how much I regret

91
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,040
not going home with her that day.

92
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:40,079
I should've gone home with her.

93
00:04:40,079 --> 00:04:40,959
Wherever she went,

94
00:04:40,959 --> 00:04:42,720
I should've gone with her.

95
00:04:44,279 --> 00:04:46,120
I should've gone home with her.

96
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,160
Bad boy!

97
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,600
Did you bully Wen?

98
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,399
Go now!

99
00:04:54,199 --> 00:04:55,000
Don't be afraid.

100
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,439
Mom's here.

101
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,720
No one will bully you.

102
00:05:13,519 --> 00:05:14,240
Qin Ming.

103
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,040
All these years,

104
00:05:19,839 --> 00:05:21,639
I've had the same dream over and over.

105
00:05:21,879 --> 00:05:22,680
What dream?

106
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,160
Maybe next time.

107
00:05:26,279 --> 00:05:27,759
I'll tell you when we meet again.

108
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:31,759
See you next time.

109
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:48,000
(Fan A 65523)

110
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:55,439
(Run...)

111
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:01,040
The fingerprint on the window board
indeed matches Le Tianyi.

112
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,240
We've figured out his background.

113
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,439
He's not a local.

114
00:06:04,439 --> 00:06:06,199
He came here ten years ago
to make a living.

115
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,680
He started out as a deliveryman.

116
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,360
No education, no connections.

117
00:06:09,439 --> 00:06:11,240
How did a delivery guy like him

118
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,160
make VP at Sun Group?

119
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,720
It was all thanks to Wang Xuan.

120
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:17,279
She's a Longfan native,

121
00:06:17,279 --> 00:06:19,040
got divorced and had a child.

122
00:06:19,319 --> 00:06:20,680
So he married her.

123
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,839
Then, through her family's connections,

124
00:06:23,839 --> 00:06:25,319
he worked his way up.

125
00:06:26,519 --> 00:06:28,120
A classic social climber.

126
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:30,360
Someone like him

127
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,040
must be deeply insecure

128
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,879
and desperate to prove himself.

129
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:38,519
With a strong female boss like Su Shi,

130
00:06:38,639 --> 00:06:40,240
he must've really resented her.

131
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,279
To her face,

132
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:43,079
he was both jealous and afraid,

133
00:06:43,079 --> 00:06:44,759
and showed her great respect.

134
00:06:45,439 --> 00:06:46,360
But behind her back,

135
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,439
who knows how many times
he betrayed her.

136
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,160
Are the shoeprints at the scene

137
00:06:51,279 --> 00:06:52,519
also Le Tianyi's?

138
00:06:53,879 --> 00:06:54,879
The size matches.

139
00:06:54,879 --> 00:06:56,120
They're all size 44.

140
00:06:56,439 --> 00:06:57,560
According to our interviews,

141
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,079
he often goes hiking in Fengshan.

142
00:06:59,079 --> 00:07:00,040
He knows the area well.

143
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,519
Could he be the Executer?

144
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,480
That fingerprint's too clean.

145
00:07:06,519 --> 00:07:08,680
Someone who claims to be the Executer

146
00:07:08,959 --> 00:07:09,920
would slip up like that?

147
00:07:09,959 --> 00:07:11,879
Mr. Dong, you mean...?

148
00:07:12,279 --> 00:07:13,319
Find out

149
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:16,399
whether that fingerprint was a slip-up

150
00:07:16,399 --> 00:07:18,279
or an attempt to mislead us.

151
00:07:18,279 --> 00:07:19,279
Either way,

152
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,480
we'll summon Le Tianyi
first thing tomorrow.

153
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,639
Who the heck are you?

154
00:07:30,439 --> 00:07:31,319
Who are you?

155
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,439
Let me go.

156
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,560
I'm talking to you!

157
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,160
Let me go!

158
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,079
Le Tianyi,

159
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,040
I suggest you stay still.

160
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:43,040
Otherwise,

161
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:46,279
I guarantee you'll see Su Shi very soon.

162
00:07:51,279 --> 00:07:52,680
Let me go!

163
00:07:52,759 --> 00:07:54,160
Let me go!

164
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,560
I'm talking to you!

165
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,360
Let me go. Now!

166
00:07:58,519 --> 00:07:59,600
I said...

167
00:08:36,159 --> 00:08:37,039
Look here.

168
00:08:56,639 --> 00:08:57,519
What's wrong?

169
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,919
You look so pale.

170
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,960
Where did I go last night?

171
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,720
You don't remember?

172
00:09:06,039 --> 00:09:08,120
We were home celebrating Niu's birthday.

173
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,159
Look.

174
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:18,080
Happy birthday!

175
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:20,519
Happy birthday to me!

176
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,039
Happy birthday!

177
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,240
Where's Niu?

178
00:09:28,559 --> 00:09:30,879
I took her to her grandma's.

179
00:09:30,879 --> 00:09:31,559
Yesterday...

180
00:09:32,399 --> 00:09:35,080
I was home? Didn't go out?

181
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,480
Didn't go anywhere?

182
00:09:37,799 --> 00:09:38,600
You didn't.

183
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:44,879
Who do you want?

184
00:09:44,919 --> 00:09:45,720
You.

185
00:09:46,759 --> 00:09:48,080
Come with us.

186
00:09:48,559 --> 00:09:49,559
Last night,

187
00:09:49,559 --> 00:09:52,480
I was home with my wife,
celebrating our girl's birthday.

188
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:55,200
There are videos and photos on my phone.

189
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,039
Look for yourself.

190
00:09:58,759 --> 00:10:00,320
Then explain to me

191
00:10:00,759 --> 00:10:02,080
why your fingerprints

192
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,639
and shoeprints

193
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,519
were found at Su Shi's crime scene.

194
00:11:12,159 --> 00:11:13,519
Le Tianyi, I'm talking to you!

195
00:11:25,679 --> 00:11:26,480
Feeding the cats.

196
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,759
I was there to feed the cats.

197
00:11:28,759 --> 00:11:30,080
That isn't a crime, right?

198
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,799
As far as I know,

199
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,840
you and Su Shi didn't get along.

200
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,120
Yet you fed her cats?

201
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,399
There are bound to be conflicts at work.

202
00:11:38,879 --> 00:11:40,120
We were just putting on a show.

203
00:11:40,639 --> 00:11:42,440
Sometimes one plays the good cop

204
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,039
and the other the bad cop.

205
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,080
Oh, right.

206
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,600
I'm allergic

207
00:11:47,399 --> 00:11:48,480
to cat hair.

208
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,600
So I made sure to wear gloves.

209
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,320
Then why would there

210
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:56,200
be my fingerprints?

211
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:56,840
Also,

212
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,600
you mentioned

213
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:59,279
the shoeprints, right?

214
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,480
They were from this pair, size 44.

215
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,159
They were my prints.

216
00:12:03,159 --> 00:12:04,039
Le Tianyi,

217
00:12:04,519 --> 00:12:05,840
watch your attitude.

218
00:12:06,039 --> 00:12:07,600
Show some respect.

219
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:08,440
Oh,

220
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,360
my bad.

221
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,240
I was worked up.

222
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,799
They were from my shoes.

223
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,440
I admit it, of course.

224
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,320
That's my shoe size,

225
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,519
(Sound Laws, Strict Enforcement)
size 44.

226
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:19,240
(Fair Justice, Universal Compliance)
But I don't think it's fair to say

227
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,759
that just because my shoeprints

228
00:12:21,759 --> 00:12:24,120
and my fingerprints were there,

229
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,879
I'm involved in this case.

230
00:12:25,879 --> 00:12:26,519
I mean,

231
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,279
you can't just say that, right?

232
00:12:31,159 --> 00:12:31,960
All right.

233
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:33,840
We'll stop here for today.

234
00:12:35,279 --> 00:12:36,799
Can I go now?

235
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:38,840
Sure.

236
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,279
(Contact Card)
Officer Han Liang.

237
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:41,320
If you think of anything else,

238
00:12:41,919 --> 00:12:42,840
give me a call anytime.

239
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:43,480
Sure.

240
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:44,799
I'm leaving.

241
00:12:44,799 --> 00:12:45,720
Watch your attitude.

242
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,480
Okay. Sorry.

243
00:13:04,159 --> 00:13:05,840
Why is there a flower?

244
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:07,879
You brought it home.

245
00:13:08,879 --> 00:13:10,279
Why would I bring this home?

246
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,639
Are you too tired?

247
00:13:12,919 --> 00:13:14,519
You did bring it home.

248
00:13:15,399 --> 00:13:17,440
Why would I bring this home?

249
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:18,519
Look at it!

250
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,440
Why would I bring it home?

251
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:21,919
This lousy thing!

252
00:13:28,159 --> 00:13:29,600
Come here!

253
00:13:30,519 --> 00:13:32,039
Look at it.

254
00:13:32,159 --> 00:13:33,159
No words.

255
00:13:33,159 --> 00:13:34,080
Listen to me.

256
00:13:34,759 --> 00:13:35,559
Tell me.

257
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,759
Where did it come from?

258
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,519
You really brought it home.

259
00:13:38,519 --> 00:13:39,279
No way!

260
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:40,480
Nonsense!

261
00:13:40,559 --> 00:13:42,440
Tell me. Where did it come from?

262
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,240
You really brought it home!

263
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,080
You really did.

264
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,279
You did.

265
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,679
Tell me. Where did it come from?

266
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,639
Tell me! Where did it come from?

267
00:13:51,799 --> 00:13:55,120
You really brought it home.

268
00:14:15,279 --> 00:14:16,080
Who is it?

269
00:14:16,279 --> 00:14:17,080
Delivery.

270
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,879
Coming.

271
00:14:30,919 --> 00:14:32,240
The flowers you ordered.

272
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,159
Happy birthday.

273
00:14:33,159 --> 00:14:34,039
Get lost!

274
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,000
Sir?

275
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:40,679
Sir?

276
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,320
Your sunflowers!

277
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,919
Thanks for coming so late.

278
00:14:57,639 --> 00:14:59,080
I just made some soup.

279
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,480
Have some before it gets cold.

280
00:15:00,519 --> 00:15:01,399
Thank you, Ms. Song.

281
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:05,919
Well,

282
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:08,440
my condition comes and goes.

283
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,440
I don't even remember

284
00:15:10,559 --> 00:15:12,279
what I was like
the last time you saw me.

285
00:15:12,399 --> 00:15:13,639
Don't mind me.

286
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,320
Of course not.

287
00:15:15,879 --> 00:15:17,320
I know all about your condition.

288
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:20,679
By the way, is Keke home?

289
00:15:23,519 --> 00:15:25,000
You're not here to see me.

290
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,840
You're here to see Keke, aren't you?

291
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,200
She's working at the supermarket.

